          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            There are many nice properties of alternating
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multilinear+function"} multilinear
            functions. So suppose that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            over a
            %span.newWikiWord
              base rig
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/base+rig"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            and that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is a multilinear function from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero"} zero
            element of the module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            as the basepoint
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            itself, we speak of an
            %strong alternating form
            (a phrase which is usually taken to include multilinearity).
          %p
            We will sometimes want to assume that scalar multiplication by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            is cancellable in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            (which for example is always the case when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            is invertible in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            other than
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vec{z}
            to represent all of the other arguments.
          #alterationImpliesAntisymmetry.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              An alternating
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multilinear+function"} multilinear function
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  antisymmetric
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/antisymmetric+function"} ?
          .proof
            %p By multilinearity,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x+y,x+y,\vec{z}) = f(x,x,\vec{z}) + f(x,y,\vec{z}) + f(y,x,\vec{z}) + f(y,y,\vec{z}) .
            %p Applying alternation, most of these terms vanish:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo +
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mn 0
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 = 0 + f(x,y,\vec{z}) + f(y,x,\vec{z}) + 0 .
            %p Therefore,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x,y,\vec{z}) + f(y,x,\vec{z}) = 0 ,
            %p which is antisymmetry.
          #antisymmetryImpliesAlternation.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              If multiplication by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              is cancellable in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %span.newWikiWord
                antisymmetric
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/antisymmetric+function"} ?
              function to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is alternating.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p By antisymmetry,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x,x,\vec{z}) + f(x,x,\vec{z}) = 0 ,
            %p or equivalently
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mn 0
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 f(x,x,\vec{z}) = 2 \cdot 0 .
            %p
              Cancelling
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x,x,\vec{z}) = 0 ,
            %p which is alternation.
          #antisymmetryWarning.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              It is false in both directions to state in general that alternating functions and antisymmetric functions are the same, but for different reasons. An alternating function must be antisymmetric
              %em if
              it is multilinear, regardless of the behaviour of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              %em if
              multiplication by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              is cancellable in the target, regardless of linearity, but not when
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              is noncancellable.
            %p The simplest strongest-possible counterexamples are
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi y
                    %mo −
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y \mapsto |y-x|)\colon \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R} ,
            %p which is alternating but not antisymmetric, and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mn 2
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y \mapsto x y)\colon \mathbb{F}_2^2 \to \mathbb{F}_2 ,
            %p which is antisymmetric but not alternating.
            %p
              Of course, alternating and antisymmetric functions
              %em are
              the same in the context of multilinear functions to a module in which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              is cancellable, in particular for multilinear functions between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+fields"} vector fields
              over the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/alternating+groups"} alternating groups
              are really about antisymmetric functions rather than alternating functions as such. (Whereas a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+function"} symmetric function
              is preserved by the application of any element of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              (in which multiplication by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              is as uncancellable as possible).
          %h2#constructive_aspects Constructive aspects
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+equality"} decidable equality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            (which is most common) or even a (possibly infinite)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+natural+number"} extended natural number
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inequality"} inequality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            there is zero. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are also equipped with inequalities, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is
            %strong strongly alternating
            if, whenever its value is inequal to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(a,b) \ne 0
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \ne b
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tight+relation"} tight
            (so that its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            in
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            in general.
